<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Early Le dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">980 CE – 1009 CE · capital Hoa Lu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short Vietnamese dynasty of Le Hoan, who repelled a Song Chinese invasion in 981 and sacked the Cham capital the following year.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 980, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> prepared to invade <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dinh-dynasty">Dai Co Viet</a> after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang">Dinh Tien Hoang</a>, the commander-in-chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Le Hoan</a> took the throne with the backing of the queen mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duong-van-nga">Duong Van Nga</a>. He ruled as Le Dai Hanh from the old Dinh capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-lu">Hoa Lu</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Le Dai Hanh</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> invasion at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chi-lang-pass">Chi Lang</a> and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bach-dang-river">Bach Dang</a> river in 981, then restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tributary-system">tributary relations</a> with the Song. In 982 he attacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/champa">Champa</a> and sacked its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indrapura-champa">Indrapura</a>. He promoted agriculture with a royal ploughing ceremony, built roads and canals, and relied on Buddhist monks as advisers and envoys.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Le Dai Hanh's</a> death in 1005 his sons fought over the succession. The last ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-long-dinh">Le Long Dinh</a>, was remembered as cruel, and on his death in 1009 the court official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-thai-to">Ly Cong Uan</a> was chosen as king, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ly-dynasty">Ly dynasty</a>, which moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/early-le-dynasty.jpg" alt="Early Le dynasty" width="320" height="345"><figcaption>Image: Night Lantern · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnam_(1009-1225).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>980 CE – 1009 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hoa Lu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Le Dai Hanh, Le Long Dinh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Vietnamese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dai Co Viet, Tiền Lê, Former Le dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=994&amp;focus=early-le-dynasty" aria-label="Early Le dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7536 1428 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Early Le dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7856 1684L7856 1684M7856 1684L7901 1174M7856 1684L7846 1656"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7856 1684h0M7901 1174h0M7846 1656h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7856 1684h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7856 1684h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=994&amp;focus=early-le-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
